### Member Portal Auth API Testing
### Use REST Client extension in VSCode or import to Postman

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000
@email = justin@imud.com
@password = password123

###############################################
# 1. Member Login
###############################################

### Login Request
# @name memberLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/member/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

### Extract token from response
@authToken = {{memberLogin.response.body.token}}

###############################################
# 2. Get Member Profile (Authenticated)
###############################################

### Get Member Profile
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/member/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

###############################################
# 3. Get Member Profile (Using Cookie)
###############################################

### Get Member Profile (cookie-based)
# Note: Cookie is automatically set from login response
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/member/auth/me

###############################################
# 4. Member Logout
###############################################

### Logout Request
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/member/auth/logout
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

###############################################
# Error Cases
###############################################

### Login with wrong password
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/member/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "wrongpassword"
}

### Login with non-existent email
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/member/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "nonexistent@test.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

### Get profile without token (should fail)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/member/auth/me

### Get profile with invalid token
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/member/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer invalid.token.here
